      "message": "Is there any reading material to understand what AP code uses vs. firmware. My understanding is that the RO image of the firmware does not change; however, the RW image changes. I am not sure I understand how the AP comes into the play here (I assume through host commands? and how the command versions come into play)\n\nThe image capture mode is set in two situations:\n1) [fpcapture](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/common/fpsensor/fpsensor_debug.cc;l\u003d137?q\u003dplatform%2Fec%20command_fpcapture\u0026ss\u003dchromiumos%2Fchromiumos%2Fcodesearch#:~:text\u003d136-,137,-138), which is a console command\n2) [cmd_fp_mode](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/util/ectool.cc;l\u003d1922?q\u003dectool.cc\u0026ss\u003dchromiumos%2Fchromiumos%2Fcodesearch#:~:text\u003d1921-,1922,-1923), which is an ectool command.\n\nSo it does not seem there is any host command that is used to set the capture image mode.",
